Let $G$ be a group and $\theta\in\operatorname{Aut}(G)$ such that $\theta^m={\sf id}$. We then define the following two sets:
\begin{align*}
H &= G^\theta=\{g\in G\mid \theta(g)=g\}\\
Q &=\{g\in G\mid g=x\theta(x)^{-1} \mbox{ for some } x\in G\}.
\end{align*}

