The following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\theta \in \operatorname{Aut}(D_\infty)$ has finite order, 
then $\theta = -x + b$ for some integer $b$.
\item $-x + b \sim -x + d$ if and only if $b \equiv d \pmod{2}$.
\end{enumerate}

